  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development by reason of its scale, design and appearance would be over dominant, inappropriate and incongruous to the established character and appearance of the conservation area. It would also fail to be subservient or incidental to the main use of the dwellinghouse. It would therefore result in less than substantial harm to the character and appearance of the conservation area and there are no public benefits to outweigh the identified harm. The proposed development is therefore contrary to the NPPF (2024), the London Plan Policy HC1, Local Plan policies LP1, LP3 and LP5, the Wandsworth Housing SPD (2016) and the Totterdown Fields Conservation Area Appraisal and Management Strategy.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development, by reason of its scale, design and location would result in an unneighbourly form of development that harms the amenity of the neighbouring occupiers in the form of loss outlook, being overbearing and presenting visual intrusion. The proposal therefore fails to comply with policy LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the Wandsworth Housing SPD (2016). \r\n",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to work with the applicant in a positive and proactive manner and the Council has, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
